ECCDA DISCUSSIONS

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE LAS VEGAS NV

424 PM PDT THU AUG 7 2025



#####################################################################

##                                                                 ##

##            DISCUSSIONS FROM THE LATEST FWF BELOW                ##

##                                                                 ##

#####################################################################



...DISCUSSION FROM RNOFWFVEF...



A COMBINATION OF SOUTH TO SOUTHWEST WINDS WITH  GUSTS AROUND 30 MPH

AND SINGLE DIGIT MINIMUM HUMIDITY CREATE  CRITICAL FIRE WEATHER

CONDITIONS IN LINCOLN COUNTY THIS AFTERNOON. FIRE WEATHER CONCERNS

DECREASE OVER THE NEXT FEW DAYS AS WINDS  SLOWLY WEAKEN. HOWEVER,

MINIMUM HUMIDITY WILL REMAIN IN THE TEENS  TO SINGLE DIGITS THROUGH

THE MIDDLE OF NEXT WEEK AND  PRECIPITATION IS NOT EXPECTED.





...DISCUSSION FROM LAXFWFSGX...





A GRADUAL COOLING TREND WILL RESULT IN HIGH TEMPERATURES FALLING  BY

5 TO 10 DEGREES OVER THE NEXT WEEK. BY THURSDAY HIGH  TEMPERATURES

WILL BE A FEW TO AROUND 5 DEGREES BELOW AVERAGE FOR  THE COAST,

VALLEYS, AND MOUNTAINS AND A FEW DEGREES ABOVE AVERAGE  FOR THE

DESERTS. THE MARINE LAYER WILL STAY QUITE SHALLOW INTO  FRIDAY,

DEEPENING SLIGHTLY TO AROUND 1500 FEET FOR THE WEEKEND  INTO NEXT

WEEK. LOWEST RELATIVE HUMIDITY FOR THE DESERTS ONTO THE  DESERT

SLOPES OF THE MOUNTAINS WILL BE 10 TO 15 PERCENT FOR FRIDAY INTO

NEXT WEEK. LOW RELATIVE HUMIDITY VALUES COMBINED WITH THE  USUAL

AFTERNOON SEA BREEZE WINDS WILL RESULT IN ELEVATED FIRE  WEATHER

CONDITIONS ON THE DESERT MOUNTAIN SLOPES.





...DISCUSSION FROM PHXFWFPSR...





TEMPERATURES WILL COOL SLIGHTLY THROUGH SATURDAY AS MOISTURE

INCREASES OVER THE REGION. DESPITE THE MOISTURE INCREASE,

THUNDERSTORMS WILL BE RELEGATED TO MAINLY HIGHER TERRAIN AREAS OF

EASTERN ARIZONA WITH LIMITED CHANCES OF WETTING RAINFALL AND 

ENHANCED CHANCES OF DRY LIGHTNING AND NEW FIRE STARTS. MINIMUM

AFTERNOON HUMIDITY LEVELS WILL IMPROVE TO A 15-20% RANGE WHILE

OVERNIGHT RECOVERY INCREASE INTO A 25-60% RANGE. WINDS WILL  RETAIN

AN AFTERNOON UPSLOPE COMPONENT WITH GUSTS TO 15-20 MPH COMMON. 





