434

FXUS64 KEWX 072327 CCA

AFDEWX



Area Forecast Discussion...CORRECTED

National Weather Service Austin/San Antonio TX

627 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Seasonably hot August temperatures and heat indices



- Slight chances (15-30%) for afternoon showers and thunderstorms

  mainly over the Coastal Plains this weekend into early next week



&&



.SHORT TERM...

(Tonight through Friday night)

Issued at 1222 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Subtropical ridge continues to stay parked over New Mexico through 

Friday. Subsidence under this ridge along with a continued dry 

airmass should limit the potential for rain with the exception of 

Lavaca and DeWitt counties as the seabreeze makes its way westward in

the afternoon. Otherwise expect seasonably hot temperatures in the 

upper 90s to low 100s for Friday with heat indices remaining below 

advisory levels but will still be hot over most areas. 



&&



.LONG TERM...

(Saturday through Thursday)

Issued at 1222 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Eventually by this weekend this subtropical ridge slowly pushes off 

to the west and somewhat flattens/weakens due to the combination of 

a strong upper level trough across the northern plains and

mississippi valley and an incoming inverted trough making its way 

westward from the southeast states. The affect this has on our area 

should be minimal besides a "cooling" of high temperatures by a 

degree or two with heat indices still elevated around the 100-105 

range as this trough tries to bring in a more moist airmass. This 

brings higher chances for afternoon coastal showers and storms mainly

staying east of the I-35 corridor and in the Coastal plains during 

the afternoon hours for the weekend. 



Looking ahead towards early next week, some global models are 

suggesting this inverted trough lingers off the TX Coast and forms 

into a coastal low swinging northward through our area. Do to some 

model agreement in this scenario decided to raise pops albeit it 

slightly to 20% across most of the area for monday afternoon. We will

have to watch this low closely due to weak steering currents as our 

area will be sandwiched between the weakening high to our west and a

developing high in the southeastern Gulf states. Continued chances 

for afternoon showers and storms resumes for the rest of the period 

mainly for the Coastal Plains. Temperatures remain seasonably hot 

with highs in the mid to upper 90s and heat indices in the 100-105 

range with lows generally remaining in the low to mid 70s. 



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 624 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Thin smoke remains above FL010 with minor reductions to slant range 

visibility but no impacts at surface. VFR prevails at all terminals. 

Not expecting a strong seabreeze tonight given earlier prevailing 

southerly flow, but have added a TEMPO for a brief uptick in winds at

DRT between 07Z and 09Z. VFR is expected through the forecast 

period, though some low clouds could develop near SSF and areas 

southeast after 09Z. Light southeasterly winds 7 to 10 kts return 

tomorrow. 



