628 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025 /728 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025/



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for portions of north central

Illinois...northeast Illinois and northwest Indiana.



.DAY ONE...Tonight.



Weather hazards expected...



 Limited Thunderstorm Risk.



DISCUSSION...



There is a 20 percent chance of a thunderstorm this evening and

overnight. Most areas will stay dry. 



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday.



Friday Morning...

  Limited Thunderstorm Risk.

Friday Afternoon through Saturday...

  Limited Excessive Heat Risk.

Late Saturday through Wednesday...

  Limited Thunderstorm Risk at times.

  Limited Flooding Risk at times.



DISCUSSION...



Hot and humid conditions are expected Friday and Saturday with 

peak afternoon heat indices up to around 100 degrees likely.



Additional periods of thunderstorms are possible late day

Saturday through mid next week.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



  Spotter activation will not be necessary through tonight.



GENERAL STORM MOTION OF THE DAY:



  Moving toward the east southeast around 20 mph.



