603

FXUS64 KSHV 072328

AFDSHV



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Shreveport LA

628 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Issued at 1212 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



 - Temperatures will remain in the mid to upper 90s throughout the

   weekend and continue into the middle of next week



 - A Heat Advisory has been issued for much of east Texas,

   northwest Louisiana, southeast Oklahoma and southwest Arkansas

   for Friday

 

 - Dry conditions will remain in place for the majority of the

   region through next week, with minimal 7-day QPF totals



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1212 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Upper-air analysis early this afternoon continues to show a ridge

centered over New Mexico, with our region on the eastern

peripheral of the ridge. This pattern will remain fairly stagnant

through the upcoming weekend and as a result, temperatures will

remain elevated with dry conditions prevailing throughout. While

we have been flirting with Heat Advisory criteria for the past day

or two, including today, I think we will see more widespread 105s

tomorrow so I have elected to issue a Heat Advisory for all of our

east Texas counties, portions of northwest Louisiana, southwest

Arkansas and then McCurtain County from 11am Friday through 7pm

Friday. There is some potential this could get extended into

portions of the area on Saturday, but we will address this with a

later forecast package. 



From Saturday onward, it looks like things are going to remain

hot, with temperatures remaining in the mid to upper 90s through

at least next Wednesday. There are some low end chances for

precipitation late in the weekend and into next week, but overall

QPF amounts will be low. WPC is only advertising up to a tenth of

an inch of total rainfall over the next 7 days for portions of the

area, with most of the area at no rainfall. Naturally, this will

force us to be extra vigilant about flash drought and some fire 

weather concerns in the future. /33/



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 621 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



The pattern continues across the airspace as the afternoon CU

field is quickly dissipating, with SKC prevailing through the

overnight period. Terminal winds will decrease through the

overnight, with more of a VRB theme around 3kts for many. By 

sunrise, SKC is expected through the morning and early afternoon 

ahead of the return of another CU field around 18z, hanging around

5kft. Once again, S/SE winds are expected at the terminals, 

averaging around 5kts. 



KNAPP



&&



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...

Issued at 1135 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Spotter activation should not be needed for days to come. 



&&



