Issued at 1142 AM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025

Winds will increase this afternoon gusting to nearly 35 mph at

most terminals, with some lighter gusts in favorable valley

locales. Clouds will remain high based as some weak moisture

streams across the Great Basin. An isolated shower can't be

ruled out across the San Juans, although this will likely just

be some virga with gusty outflow winds beneath it. VFR

conditions continue overnight, while winds will subside around

dark. Stronger winds on Friday are expected to get an earlier

start given that we remain well mixed overnight in the valleys.





