AFDJAN



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service Jackson MS

630 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1258 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Typical summertime weather conditions are expected across our 

forecast area into late next week. A stout upper-level ridge of high 

pressure over the Desert Southwest will break down over the next few 

days and allow a more zonal flow pattern to develop over the 

northern CONUS. To the south, a tropical wave will bring the return 

of easterly flow and deeper 2+ inch PWAT air to our region. This 

will result in  better rain chances and more humidity by the early 

parts of next week. At this time, it appears that some parts of the 

forecast area could end up with dangerous heat stress conditions 

(heat index >105), but rain chances limit confidence of heat impacts 

at this time. /NF/



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 630 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



VFR flight categories will prevail at area TAF sites through much

of this 00Z forecast package. There will be a 2-4 hour period 

around day break Friday, where categories could briefly fall to 

MVFR categories due to patchy shallow ground fog. This will 

quickly erode after sunrise, with VFR yet again prevailing. Winds 

will subside this evening, remaining calm to light from the east 

around 3 knots overnight into Friday morning. /19/



