Including the Communities of Key Largo, Marathon, and Key West

733 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.NOW...

Through 900 pm, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms will 

wax and wane as they move generally to the southwest at near 10 knots

through the Florida Keys waters. Mariners encountering the stronger 

activity, currently located south of the Dry Tortugas, can expect 

brief heavy downpours reducing visibility, wind gusts of 20 to 25 

knots with a possible 25 to 30 knot gust, and a few cloud to surface 

lightning strikes. Island communities, especially in the Lower Keys, 

may observe a an additional tenth of an inch of rainfall.



$$



