=================================================



682

FXUS62 KTBW 072334

AFDTBW



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Tampa Bay Ruskin FL

734 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Showers and storms continue near coastal terminals to keep Tempo

groups for MVFR briefly IFR cigs/vsbys with gusty winds in stronger

cells through around 02Z then short lived light VCSH possible 

before clearing around midnight with VFR conditions overnight into

Fri morning with light easterly winds. Fri aft 18Z expect

seabreeze development and afternoon TSRA at or nr all terminals. 



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 149 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025 



Low-level flow has switched to more northeast to east this 

afternoon as a weak boundary remains stalled over north Florida. 

This has led to showers and thunderstorms developing from the east

coast and interior earlier to now shifting toward the Gulf coast 

through this afternoon and evening. The setup will be very similar

for Friday, with the best storm chances near the coast later in 

the day. Rain chances then go up a bit for the weekend with 

moisture on the rise, though flow will be more southeasterly. 



For next week, boundary layer winds generally stay out of the east 

to southeast. Overall, no major pattern changes, just some subtle 

differences in moisture resulting in different rain chances each 

day. 



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 149 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025 



East to southeast winds will remain over the waters through the next 

several days, with a turn onshore near the coast each afternoon. The 

best rain chances for today and Friday will be later in the evening 

as convection moves westward over the waters from land, then rain 

chances increase for the weekend. 



&&



.FIRE WEATHER...

Issued at 149 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025 



No fire weather concerns for the next several days as relative 

humidity values will remain above critical levels. Warm and humid 

summertime conditions will continue, with scattered showers and 

thunderstorms each day, generally moving from east to west through 

the day. 



&&



