=================================================



690

FXUS63 KUNR 072334

AFDUNR



Area Forecast Discussion For Western SD and Northeastern WY

National Weather Service Rapid City SD

534 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Hot this afternoon into early evening with heat indices 100-105F 

  across south central SD

- Marginal to slight (level 1-2 of 5) risk of severe thunderstorms

  tonight and Friday afternoon/evening

- Seasonally drier for the weekend into early next week



&&



.DISCUSSION...(This Evening Through Thursday)

Issued at 215 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025



For the 20Z upper level analysis, ridging is present across the

Central Plains, with a large trof across the Pacific Northwest.

Southwest upper flow is present across the Northern Plains, with

skies mostly sunny at the moment. A few weak showers with some

isolated lightning have just developed this afternoon across far

southwestern SD.



At the surface, a strong dry line has pushed into the far 

southwest corner of the forecast area, with dewpoints in the 30s

south of the line, compared to mid to upper 60s elsewhere.

Temperatures range from the 80s to the north, to the low 100s

across southern SD. Winds are mainly out of the southeast across

the SD plains, to the north to northeast from the Black Hills area

into northeastern WY. Breezy west to southwest winds are present

south of the aforementioned dry line. Current highlights will

expire early this evening.



Ridging across the Central Plains will break down tonight as a 

strong cold front moves across the area. Weak convection across

far southern SD will shift east through the evening. Anticipated

strong storms over North Dakota this evening and overnight look to

remain north of the area per latest CAMs. Outflow from these

storms could push the cold front through the forecast area a

little quicker overnight.



Upper trof swings into central Montana by Friday as surface cold

front slides completely through the area. Along with the cooler

temperatures, gusty northwesterly winds are expected across the SD

plains, with gusts to 35 mph possible. High temperatures will 

range from near 70 degrees in northeast WY to near 90 degrees in

far south central SD. Some isolated rain showers and thunderstorms

will be possible across the area.



Upper trof lifts into Canada by the weekend as area resides under

mainly dry west to northwest flow. Temperatures will rebound over

the weekend into the middle of next week as a broad area of high

pressure slides from the Northern Rockies into the Northern

Plains. Temperatures will mainly be in the upper 70s and 80s over

the weekend, warming to the 80s and 90s by early next week. 



&&



.AVIATION...(For the 00Z TAFS Through 00Z Friday Evening)

Issued At 533 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Mainly VFR conditions expected through the TAF period. An 

isolated TSRA will be possible from the KIEN area eastward to 

KICR early this evening. TSRA may occur tonight over northwest SD

where localized IFR conditions are expected with any storm. A 

cold front will move through the area tonight, with gusty 

northwest winds to 35 knots expected across the SD plains from 06Z

through the remainder of the TAF period.



&&



.UNR WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

SD...Heat Advisory until 7 PM MDT /8 PM CDT/ this evening for SDZ014-

     032-043-046-047-049-077.

     Red Flag Warning until 8 PM MDT this evening for SDZ322.

WY...Red Flag Warning until 8 PM MDT this evening for WYZ315.

&&



$$



DISCUSSION/KEY MESSAGES...15

AVIATION...Dye



