Hazardous Weather Outlook

National Weather Service Bismarck ND

637 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



NDZ001>005-009>013-017>023-031>036-040>046-082345-

Divide-Burke-Renville-Bottineau-Rolette-Williams-Mountrail-Ward-

McHenry-Pierce-McKenzie-Dunn-Mercer-Oliver-McLean-Sheridan-Wells-

Golden Valley-Billings-Stark-Morton-Burleigh-Kidder-Slope-

Hettinger-Grant-Bowman-Adams-Sioux-Emmons-

637 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025 /537 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025/



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for portions of north central

North Dakota, northwest North Dakota, south central North Dakota,

and southwest North Dakota.



.DAY ONE...Tonight



Scattered to numerous severe thunderstorms are expected this 

afternoon through tonight. Significant severe weather is possible,

with very large hail up to the size of baseballs, damaging winds 

as high as 80 mph, and a few tornadoes. Localized excessive

rainfall is also possible.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday



Isolated severe thunderstorms are possible on Friday, with hail as

large as quarters and wind gusts as high as 60 mph.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotters are encouraged to report any severe weather to the

National Weather Service at 701-223-4582 or to our social media

pages.



$$



NDZ025-037-047-048-050-051-082345-

Foster-Stutsman-Logan-La Moure-McIntosh-Dickey-

637 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for portions of southeast North

Dakota.



.DAY ONE...Tonight



Scattered to numerous severe thunderstorms are expected this 

afternoon through tonight. Significant severe weather is possible,

with very large hail up to the size of baseballs, damaging winds 

as high as 80 mph, and a few tornadoes. Localized excessive

rainfall is also possible.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday



Scattered severe thunderstorms are possible on Friday. Expected 

hazards include hail as large as golf balls, damaging winds up to

60 mph.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotters are encouraged to report any severe weather to the

National Weather Service at 701-223-4582 or to our social media

pages.



