=================================================



740

FXUS61 KBUF 072338

AFDBUF



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Buffalo NY

738 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.SYNOPSIS...

Surface high pressure will promote largely dry weather across 

Western New York through Friday. Heat and humidity levels begin to 

creep up over the weekend which lasts into early next week. Next 

chance of precipitation possibly Tuesday or Wednesday.



&&



.NEAR TERM /THROUGH FRIDAY/...

Dry weather will persist across the forecast area tonight.

Patchy valley fog is possible across the western Southern Tier.



High pressure will once again provide dry weather across much of the 

area through Friday. Temps will climb a few degrees, with low 

to mid 80s most locales, possibly upper 80s along the lake 

plains in spots.



&&



.SHORT TERM /FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY NIGHT/...

Surface high pressure off the Atlantic Coast will 'likely' maintain 

dry weather but will promote a slow warming trend over the weekend 

into early next week. H850T's are advertised to creep up from 

+14C/+16C to +20C/+21C by Monday. This will support highs in the 

upper 80s to low 90s, with the warmest spots found along the lake 

plains, Genesee Valley and Finger Lakes region. That said...given 

the dry antecedent conditions humidity levels are not expected to be 

all that oppressive with a few spots nearing low-end Heat Advisory 

criteria. Heat may partially linger into Tuesday with humidity 

becoming elevated depending on the timing of an approaching cold 

for Tuesday.



&&



.LONG TERM /TUESDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...

A weakening cold front is advertised to approach the region on 

Tuesday from the northwest, which may bring us more appreciable 

chances for some needed rainfall in the form of showers and 

thunderstorms. As was mentioned timing of the front remains 

uncertain with unsettle weather lasting possibly into Wednesday. 

After that...it looks like brief ridging builds in for Thursday but 

again that will all depend on the front clearing the region.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...

Prevailing VFR conditions will continue across western and 

north central NY through Friday, however there are a few

exceptions. Hazy conditions due to the smoke in the area, is

causing some stations to drop to 4-6SM. This should improve 

later tonight through Friday. Some patchy fog may be possible in

the Southern Tier late tonight, however there is a low chance 

of IFR or below. 



Outlook...



Friday through Monday...VFR.



Tuesday...Mainly VFR. A chance of a shower or thunderstorm.



&&



.MARINE...

Light southerly flow with minimal wave (< 2 feet) action on area 

lakes through Friday. Surface high pressure anchored along the 

eastern seaboard will maintain light winds through the weekend, 

fluctuating between southerly and easterly.



&&



.BUF WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

NY...None.

MARINE...None.



&&



$$



SYNOPSIS...AR

NEAR TERM...AR/HSK

SHORT TERM...AR

LONG TERM...AR/PP

AVIATION...HSK

MARINE...AR



