FXUS64 KSJT 072341 AAA

AFDSJT



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service San Angelo TX

641 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Heat Advisory Big Country Friday Noon to 8 PM...



- Hot and dry conditions through this weekend.



- Not quite as hot for Monday and Tuesday with a few isolated

  showers and storms possible.



&&



.SHORT TERM...

(This evening through Friday)

Issued at 122 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Temperatures and heat indices will approach or equal 105 in the 

Big Country along/north of I-20 Friday afternoon...thus added a 

heat advisory. Farther south, highs in the 100 to 103 range are 

expected in the Concho Valley and Coleman and Brown counties, 

with upper 90s elsewhere. 



This afternoon, a nice cumulus field had developed along the I-10

corridor. While a brief shower/thunderstorm is possible late this

afternoon, coverage will be sparse, if storms occur. Lows tonight

in the low to mid 70s expected, with the warmer readings along 

and north of I-20. 



&&



.LONG TERM...

(Friday night through next Thursday)

Issued at 137 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Saturday looks to be the last hot day for West Central Texas for

this stretch, with the dominant upper level ridge forecasted to

break down starting on Sunday. This allows temperatures to cool,

with highs in the 97 to 103 range on Saturday cooling into the mid

and upper 90s for Sunday and then low to mid 90s for Monday.

Probabilistic information reveals this trend as well, with medium

to high chances (60-90%) of 100+ degree temperatures Friday

afternoon dropping to medium chances (30-60%) by Saturday, and

then low chances (less than 20%) by Sunday afternoon. 



As mentioned yesterday, breakdown of the upper ridge for early

next week is a typical pattern where we see at least a few

isolated showers or storms across the area. Latest model blends

are showing some of this for Monday afternoon, bringing some low

POPs int the southeast portions of the area southeast of a San

Saba to Menard to Sonora line. Once we get closer and get a better

view with some of the CAMs, suspect that small POPs will be

expanded over a much larger portion of the area for Monday

afternoon. 



Models are indicating that the ridge will start to reassert itself

for later portions of next week and temperatures will start to

inch their way back towards the 100 mark in some areas once again.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 640 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



VFR conditions and clear skies will continue through the next 24

hours. South-southeast winds this evening will decrease and winds

will veer to south by late tonight. During the day Friday, south 

or south-southwest winds will increase to 8-10 knots by mid-to-

late morning at our southern terminals and continue through the

afternoon. A few higher gusts are possible at our southern

terminals. At KSJT/KABI, winds will increase to 10-14 knots by

mid-to-late morning and continue through the afternoon. Gusts to 

18-21 knots expected at times at KABI and KSJT. By late afternoon

and early evening, winds at our TAF sites will back slightly to 

the southeast or south-southeast. 



&&



