099

FNAK53 PAFG 072349

FWFAFG



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Interior Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

349 PM AKDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT FOR FIRE WEATHER ZONE 937...



.DISCUSSION...Very low RHs down into the teens this afternoon across the Upper

Tanana Valley are expected to recover well into the 80s and 90s overnight tonight.

RHs will moderate across all areas Friday as a warm front moves north over the Alaska

Range, bringing scattered showers with it. Thunderstorm activity is not expected

with it as it is a stable front from a low pressure system over Bristol Bay. An 

Arctic trough bringing cooler air to the western Interior will bring isolated 

thunderstorms to most of the area except for the Upper Tanana Valley on Saturday.

The trough will push through the Interior through Sunday, bringing 0.1"-0.25" to

most of the area, except possibly less near Tok through Monday morning. Ridging 

builds back in for Monday and Tuesday with warmer temperatures and dry conditions

before the pattern becomes very progressive with general troughing prevailing. 

This will bring cooler temperatures and more showers.



