Denver/Boulder Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2020 UTC Thursday, August  7, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS through 18Z Friday/...

Issued at 1107 AM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025

We've seen an increase in smoke this morning, but not bad enough 

to greatly impact approach visibilities. The HRRR model shows less

smoke for Friday morning, so will not include it in the TAF since

impacts are not expected. Southwest winds currently in place will

turn westerly around 21Z with gusts to 25 knots possible. Appears

there is enough mid and high level moisture for isolated high-

based showers to form later today (after 21Z). Little to no rain 

is expected to reach the ground, but gusty outflow winds may bring

a wind shift or two to the airports. Therefore will continue with

the PROB30 for gusty outflow winds. South to southwest winds will

tonight and Friday morning (06-18Z). West winds to 30 knots will 

be possible after 18Z Friday.





