Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2049 UTC Thursday, August  7, 2025



.AVIATION...

(18Z TAFS)

Issued at 246 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025

Virga showers and isolated dry thunderstorms will develop over the 

high terrain and be a nuisance over most areas outside of the 

eastern plains. Erratic and gusty winds up to 40 kts will be the 

main concern associated with these storms. The threat of virga 

showers will diminish after sunset, with wind speeds becoming more 

light and variable. Eastern sites like KTCC and KROW will see a 

steady breezy to gusty southwesterly wind continue into the evening. 

Mid and high level clouds will build during the course of the 

afternoon and persist during the overnight hours throughout the 

state. 



