Spot Forecast for Beulah Fire...Summit County Emergency Management

National Weather Service Salt Lake City UT

556 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1800 MDT on August 07. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION... Conditions continue to remain quite dry through the

remainder of today and tonight with some recovery expected Friday

afternoon ahead of a dry cold front with MinRH values in the low 

30% range. However, this will be short lived with MinRH values 

dipping back into the mid teens this weekend. Southwesterly winds

will continue through around 2100 before flow lightens resulting

in generally downcanyon winds through the remainder of the

evening. With tomorrows cold front, winds will pick up around 0900

out of the west, becoming terrain driven in the evening hours once

again. This pattern is expected to repeat itself through Saturday

with winds lightening into the weekend. 



.TONIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Partly cloudy (30-40 percent cloud cover). 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of pcpn......0 percent. 

Chance of lightning.0 percent. 

Min temperature.....Around 40. 

Max humidity........40-45 percent for lower elevations with 55-60 percent across higher elevations. 

Wind (20 ft)........Southwest winds 6-16 mph through 2100 before becoming terrain-driven downslope 3 to 6 mph. 

Gusts up to 45 mph early in the evening, primarily across ridgetops.

Mixing height.......200 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Southwest around 33 mph becoming around 14 mph 

                    overnight. 



.FRIDAY...



Sky/weather.........Mostly sunny (25-35 percent cloud cover) then 

                    becoming partly cloudy (45-55 percent cloud 

                    cover). 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of pcpn......10 percent. 

Chance of lightning.11 percent. 

Max temperature.....Around 62. 

Min humidity........31-33 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........Downslope winds 3-6 mph becoming 17-20 mph with gusts to around 28 mph 

                    beginning around 0900-1000. Gusty and erratic winds expected near thunderstorms 

                in the afternoon. 

Mixing height.......7500 ft AGL. 

   Climatology......60-70th Percentile. 

Transport winds.....West 29 to 32 mph. 



.FRIDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Mostly clear (5-15 percent cloud cover). 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of pcpn......0 percent. 

Chance of lightning.2 percent. 

Min temperature.....33-35. 

Max humidity........47-49 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........West-northwest winds 7-17 mph with gusts to around 

                    23 mph through 2100 before becoming terrain-driven downslope 3 to 6 mph. 

Gusts up to 35 mph early in the evening, primarily across ridgetops. 

Mixing height.......200 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....West around 29 mph becoming north around 7 mph 

                    overnight. 



.SATURDAY...



Sky/weather.........Mostly sunny (25-35 percent cloud cover) then 

                    becoming partly cloudy (45-55 percent cloud 

                    cover). 

CWR.................0 percent. 

