=================================================



221

FXUS64 KCRP 072357

AFDCRP



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Corpus Christi TX

657 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Updated at 611 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



- Generally low 10-30% chance of showers and thunderstorms most 

  days. Slightly higher 20-40% chances over the weekend.



- Generally minor to moderate risk of heat related impacts across 

most of South Texas. At times, a brief major risk can be expected 

across portions of the Brush Country, through the period. 



- Elevated fire weather conditions across the western Brush

  Country and Rio Grande Plains through the weekend and into next

  week.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1227 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Typical summer time conditions continue across S TX. Friday will 

be the driest day with a very low (<15%) of showers or 

thunderstorms as a mid to upper level high pressure system 

dominates S TX weather. Over the weekend there will be a low to 

medium (20-40%) chance of showers and thunderstorms along the sea 

breeze due to a mid level inverted trough moving across the region

and advecting slightly deeper moisture into the area. Daily sea 

breeze convection will continue through next week. 



Heat indices will generally be 100-109 each afternoon. A few areas 

could briefly reach around 110 as the sea breeze moves inland, but 

conditions should remain below Heat Advisory levels due to it being 

localized and brief. Generally there is minor to moderate risk of 

heat related impacts each day. A few locations across the Brush 

Country may see a brief major risk through Friday.



Elevated fire weather conditions may exist across western portions 

of Webb County due to minimum RH values forecast to be 25-30 percent 

and above normal Energy Release Component values. However, winds are 

expected to remain below thresholds through the period.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 611 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



A repeat of the last 24 hours is expected this forecast package.

Primarily VFR conditions will have brief instances of MVFR/IFR

VSBYs and CIGs from 09-13Z over the coastal sites (ALI/VCT/CRP).

Otherwise, winds will remain light with gusts around 20 knots in

the wake of the seabreeze.



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 1227 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



A light to gentle (BF 2-3) south to southeast flow is expected 

during the overnight hours then increasing to a gentle to moderate 

(BF 3-4) breeze during the afternoons and evenings each day through 

early next week. There is 10-20 percent chance of showers and 

thunderstorms Friday increasing to a 20-45 percent over the weekend 

and into Monday.



&&



.PRELIMINARY POINT TEMPS/POPS...

Corpus Christi    77  96  76  94 /   0  10   0  20 

Victoria          75  97  74  95 /   0  10   0  30 

Laredo            79 105  78 103 /   0   0   0   0 

Alice             74 100  74  97 /   0  10   0  20 

Rockport          79  93  79  92 /   0  10  10  20 

Cotulla           78 104  76 102 /   0   0   0  10 

Kingsville        74  97  74  95 /   0  10   0  20 

Navy Corpus       80  91  81  90 /   0  10  10  20 



&&



.CRP WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

TX...None.

GM...None.

&&



$$





DISCUSSION...TE/81

AVIATION...EMF/94



