429

FXUS63 KIWX 080001

AFDIWX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Northern Indiana

801 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Much more uncomfortable temperatures and humidity levels in

  store with highs in the upper 80s to near 90 and heat indices

  in the low to mid 90s into the weekend. 



- An isolated shower or storm remains possible late tonight into

  early Friday mainly along and north of the Michigan/Indiana

  state line. 



- Somewhat better chances for showers and storms return next

  week, with low confidence on timing and locations to be

  impacted.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 303 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Capping across the area has allowed for shallow cu development,

but no indications of convection. This will likely persist into

the overnight hours with some high clouds streaming in from

upstream convection. One small possible area to be watched is

along the shoreline of Lk MI where vis sat shows maybe some

slightly better developed cu on the lake breeze. Will leave dry,

but may need to watch trends over the next couple of hours. 

Challenges still exist regarding convective potential upstream 

across WI and IL, eventually into Lk MI, lower MI and possibly N

Indiana. CAMs have backed off considerably compared to past 

days with almost no development across the area as the main area

of storms develops across N Dakota and track east. Have trimmed

east/southeast extent of pops overnight into Friday and capped

at slgt chc. Suspect they could be removed all together, but

given the soupy, unstable airmass that will be in place can't

completely rule out a stray shower or storm. 



The heat and humidity will become front and center for the

upcoming weekend with highs near 90 and heat indices in the low

to mid 90s as the upper level ridge takes hold. Shower and

thunderstorm chances will return at some point next week as a

deeper trough shifts east towards the region by Tue/Wed where

the best chances for precip reside. Still low confidence on

timing and most favored locations at this point so broad slgt

chc to chc pops maintained.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SATURDAY/...

Issued at 757 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Scattered showers and thunderstorms this evening are confined

mainly to central Illinois. This location corresponds to

moderate to strong sfc based instability and favorable proximity

downstream of a southeast sinking MCV across southwest IL, and

along an old residual outflow boundary. A few isolated cells

developed over past several hours across west central IN, but

have recently diminished as loss of peak heating appears to be

already creating some weak sfc based CIN given slightly warmer

mid level thermal profiles today. 



Will continue to lean toward dry forecast at terminals tonight

with initial focus of any elevated convection probably back 

closer to IL/IN stateline near stronger theta-e gradient. The 

possibility does exist for some additional isolated/scattered 

storms to develop overnight across NE Illinois/Lake Michigan 

vicinity as a modest low level southwesterly jet provides some 

advective forcing. Some elevated moisture return may be enough 

for an isolated thunderstorm potential at KSBN, but confidence 

in occurrence and expected coverage remains too low to include. 

Low probabilities for isolated storms may exist across far 

northern Indiana into Friday, but gradually building mid level 

ridge leads to low confidence. Otherwise, fog potential seems 

more limited tonight, but cannot rule out at least some brief 

MVFR vsbys late tonight/early Friday. Some increase in southerly

gradient and steep low level lapse rates should support some 

southerly gusts to around 15 knots at KSBN Friday afternoon, 

with slightly lower speeds at KFWA.



&&



.IWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

IN...None.

OH...None.

MI...None.

MARINE...None.



&&



$$



DISCUSSION...Fisher

AVIATION...Marsili



