533

FNUS76 KLOX 080008

FWSLOX



Spot Forecast for Canyon Fire...Ventura County

National Weather Service Los Angeles/Oxnard CA

508 PM PDT Thu Aug 7 2025



If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...

High confidence in diurnal winds persisting through Friday night with

Upcanyon (south to southwest) winds during the afternoon to evening

hours, decreasing substantially by late evening and overnight and 

generally shifting to the northeast at the ridgetops. The valleys and

canyons will see light downslope/ downvalley winds overnight. High

temperatures will drop by a degree or two on Friday, with a slight

rise in minimum humidities. Overnight recoveries will likely be fair

with a slight increase Friday night compared to tonight. During the

peak heating of the day, moderate plume-dominated fire behavior will

be possible Friday afternoon into the early evening hours (1800-1900).



.TONIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Clear (0-10 percent). 

Min temperature.....65-73, warmest in the hills. 

Max humidity........45-50 percent except 40-45 in the hills. 

Eye level winds.....Upcanyon winds 4 to 6 mph with gusts up to 9 mph

                    becoming downcanyon 1 to 3 mph overnight. 

Wind (20 ft)........South to southwest/ upcanyon 8 to 12 mph with gusts

                    18 mph becoming northeast/ downcanyon 3 to 6 mph 

                    after 2300. 

Ridgetop wind.......Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph with gusts to 20 mph

                    becoming northeast 3 to 5 mph.   

Mixing height.......3300 ft AGL lowering to 900 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Southwest 10 to 15 mph becoming northeast 2 to 5 mph. 



.FRIDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny (0-10 percent). 

Max temperature.....96-99. 

Min humidity........16-19 percent. 

Eye level winds.....Downcanyon winds 2 to 3 mph becoming southwest/ upcanyon

                    5 to 7 mph with gusts 10 to 12 mph in the afternoon. 

Wind (20 ft)........Downcanyon winds 3 to 4 mph becoming southwest/ upcanyon 

                    12 to 14 mph with gusts 18 to 20 mph in the afternoon. 

Ridgetop wind.......Northeast winds 3 to 6 mph becoming southwest 10 to 15

                    mph with gusts 20 to 25 mph in the afternooon.  

Mixing height.......1000 ft AGL rising to 4500 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Light winds becoming southwest 10 to 15 mph. 



.FRIDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Clear (0-5)

Min Temperature.....65-75, warmest in the  hills. 

Max humidity........50-60 percent except 45-50 percent in the hills. 

Eye level winds.....Southwest/ upcanyon winds 3 to 6 mph with gusts to 9 mph in 

                    the evening becoming downcanyon 1 to 3 mph. 

Wind (20 ft)........Southwest/ upcanyon winds 6 to 12 mph with gusts to 18 mph in the 

                    evening becoming downcanyon 2 to 4 mph overnight. 

Ridgetop wind.......Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph with gusts to 20 mph becoming

                    northeast 3 to 5 mph.  

Mixing height.......3500 ft AGL lowering to 800 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Southwest 8 to 12 mph becoming east around 4 mph. 



$$

Forecaster...SMITH

Requested by...Ventura County

Type of request...WILDFIRE

.TAG 2519513.0/LOX

.DELDT 08/07/25

.FormatterVersion 2.0.0

.EMAIL dutyofficer@ceooem.lacounty.gov,drew.smith@fire.lacounty.gov,oes.oes@ventura.org,garrett.hazelton@fire.lacounty.gov



