Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2352 UTC Thursday, August  7, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 536 PM MDT Thu Aug 7 2025

Virga showers and dry storms will continue to decrease in coverage

through the evening, but gusty outflow winds to 40KT will remain a

possibility at all terminals through around 03Z. Light winds will

prevail around the region tonight, except for the eastern plains

where a S/SW breeze will hang on through the night. There is a low

chance of LLWS in the eastern plains at KTCC tonight between 06Z

and 12Z.

Tomorrow afternoon will be very similar to today with scattered 

showers and dry storms favoring the high terrain. Coverage will be

greatest south of I-40 and there is a low chance that storms 

develop into a semi-organized line in the eastern plains during 

the late afternoon. Gusty and erratic outflow winds will remain 

the main aviation concern through the TAF period.



