Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Springfield MO

727 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- A Heat Advisory has been issued for mostly along and west of

  Highway 65 for Friday from 1-8 PM. Hot and humid conditions

  across the area into the weekend. Afternoon temperatures in 

  the lower to middle 90s, with heat index values approaching 

  100 degrees.



- Additional chances late Saturday into Sunday, persisting into

  next week. No widespread chances at this time.



&&



.SHORT TERM /THROUGH TONIGHT/...

Issued at 311 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



A dying MCS has moved its way into eastern MO this afternoon

brining cloud cover, cooler temperatures, and a few

thunderstorms/rain showers. These showers should dissipate in

the next hour or so and temperatures will warm up into the upper

80s over in the eastern Ozarks. The rest of our area is

currently in the lower 90s and will top out in the mid 90s over

the next couple of hours. Winds will stay elevated gusting to 25

mph this afternoon but will diminish this evening. Cloud cover 

will continue to dissipate and skies will clear out this 

evening. Tonight, expect warm temperatures in the upper 60s to 

lower 70s.



&&



.LONG TERM /FRIDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...

Issued at 311 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



A heat advisory has been issued for Friday 1-8pm for areas

primarily west of Highway 65 for heat indices reaching 106

degrees tomorrow. Be sure to drink plenty of water and take

frequent breaks if working outside. 



Friday-Sunday: The upper-level ridge builds into late

week/weekend with increasing mid-level heights. This will

support temperatures a few degrees warmer on Friday and 

Saturday, with highs varying from lower 90s (east) to 

middle/upper 90s (west). Maximum afternoon heat index values are

progged to reach into the upper 90s to around 100 once. Another

heat advisory may be issued for Saturday, but that will be

evaluated in the overnight forecast update. Meanwhile, PoPs 

remain minimal (<10%) through Saturday evening, with dry 

conditions expected to prevail.



By Saturday night into Sunday, a slight breakdown in the ridge

occurs as a trough translates across the Northern Plains. This

will support the return of additional rain chances (10-20%)

across west central and central MO. Confidence remains low on

any widespread rainfall chances through the weekend.



Next Week: The general trend supports temperatures remaining 

near normal to a few degrees above normal as we head into mid-

August. This would be characterized by daily highs in the lower 

90s. While there is some uncertainty depicted in the ensembles, 

the pattern appears to support daily rain chances (10-30%) as it

becomes quasi- zonal in nature. Future forecast updates will 

work to pin down the best rain chances, and potential coverage.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SATURDAY/...

Issued at 721 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



VFR conditions will persist through the TAF period. Afternoon

gusty winds are expected again on Friday.



&&



.SGF WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

KS...Heat Advisory from 1 PM to 8 PM CDT Friday for KSZ073-097-101.

MO...Heat Advisory from 1 PM to 8 PM CDT Friday for MOZ055-056-

     066>069-077>080-088>091-093>095-101>104.



&&



$$



