Salt Lake City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2129 UTC Thursday, August  7, 2025



.AVIATION...KSLC...Northwesterly winds will likely prevail, with 

gusts dropping off after 01-02z this evening. Light, northwesterly 

winds will continue, though may become light and variable at times 

overnight. VFR conditions will prevail.

.REST OF UTAH AND SOUTHWEST WYOMING...A dry cold front will move 

across much of the state overnight, entering northwestern Utah 

around 00z, reaching the Wasatch Front around 06z and stalling 

around central Utah by Friday morning. Winds ahead of this front 

will continue to be strong out of the southwest each late-

morning/afternoon, with lighter, northwesterly winds behind the 

front. VIS reductions are possible near local wildfires.





