Amarillo Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2333 UTC Thursday, August  7, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 625 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025

As of early this evening, showers and thunderstorms were still

present across the western Oklahoma Panhandle and slowly moving 

east. However, these storms are struggling to maintain themselves 

and are currently unlikely to impact KGUY. Meanwhile, both KAMA 

and KDHT are both VFR and expected to stay that way through the 

overnight, albeit with some surface wind gust present. The only 

thing that may need to be watch is some slight haze from ongoing 

prescribed burns occurring one county over to the east of KAMA. 

However, wind direction should keep the smoke out of the area for

the most part.





