855 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



.NOW...

Through 1000 pm, scattered showers and and a stray thunderstorm will

wax and wane as they move generally to the west at near 10 knots 

through the Florida Keys waters. Mariners encountering the stronger 

activity can expect brief moderate to heavy downpours reducing 

visibility, wind gusts of near 20 knots, and a stray lightning 

strike. Island communities, especially in the Lower Keys, may observe

a an additional hundredth of an inch of rainfall.



