Recreation Forecast

National Weather Service Grand Forks ND

800 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Here are the Recreation Area Forecasts...



Wave height forecasts represent the average of the highest 33% of

waves that occur in a given period. Since the significant wave

height is an average of the largest waves, mariners should be

aware that many individual waves will be higher. 



For Devils Lake...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Southeast winds 10 to 20 mph shifting to the

southwest after midnight, then shifting to the north early in the

morning. Waves 1 foot or less. Scattered thunderstorms through

the night. Numerous showers after midnight. Mostly cloudy. Lows

in the mid 60s. 

.FRIDAY...West winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Scattered showers in the morning. Scattered thunderstorms through

the day. Mostly cloudy. Highs 75 to 85. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...West winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Scattered showers through the night. Mostly cloudy in the evening

then becoming partly cloudy. Lows in the upper 50s. 





For the Upper and Lower Red Lakes...



.REST OF TONIGHT...South winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or

less. Partly cloudy in the evening then becoming mostly cloudy.

Lows in the upper 60s. 

.FRIDAY...South winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Scattered thunderstorms through the day. Partly sunny. Highs

75 to 85. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...Southeast winds around 10 mph shifting to the

southwest in the late evening and overnight. Waves 1 foot or

less. Showers and numerous thunderstorms. Mostly cloudy. Lows in

the mid 60s. 





For Lake of the Woods...



.REST OF TONIGHT...Light winds becoming south around 10 mph in

the late evening and overnight. Waves 1 foot or less. Partly

cloudy in the evening then becoming mostly cloudy. Lows in the

mid 60s. 

.FRIDAY...Southeast winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Scattered thunderstorms. Partly sunny. Highs in the 70s. 

.FRIDAY NIGHT...East winds around 10 mph shifting to the

southwest after midnight. Waves 1 foot or less. Showers and

numerous thunderstorms. Mostly cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 





