FXZS60 NSTU 080103

AFDPPG



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Pago Pago  AS

203 PM SST Thu Aug 7 2025



.Short term...

Latest satellite data shows fair weather over the Islands as the

trough that brought showers yesterday has weakened. Expect

isolated to scattered showers and light winds for tonight.

However, afternoon showers are possible as a gentle breeze allows

for a sea-breeze effect to take place. By Friday, a ridge to the 

southeast will slowly build in the area. This feature will hold 

southeast trades through Saturday. Instability trends are also 

minimal for this duration, so expect isolated to scattered 

showers and little to no thunderstorm development.



.Long term...

A weak trough will develop over the territory on Sunday as winds 

shift from southeast to east. This is due to the eastward track of

the aforementioned ridge. Expect a possible uptick in showers to

numerous, with a low potential for flash flooding. As the trough

weakens Monday night, expect showers to diminish to scattered. 

East winds of 10 to 15 mph will hold through the end of the 

forecast period.





&&

.Marine...

Wave heights remain around 10 feet as a strong south swell

continues to pass through coastal waters. These heights are

evident on PacIOOS buoys, as well as peak periods near 16 

seconds. For this reason, the High Surf Warning was extended 

through tonight. Although wave heights are forecast to follow a 

diminishing trend tonight, peak periods will hold high surf and 

rip current hazards until Friday afternoon. By saturday, waves 

are forecast to diminish below advisory thresholds. However,

trades may keep textured seas through the new week. 



.PPG WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

High Surf Warning

High Surf Advisory

Small Craft Advisory



&&



$$



