804 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for south central Nebraska and

portions of north central Kansas.



.DAY ONE...Tonight.



The probability for widespread hazardous weather is low.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday.



Heat index values of 105 to 109 degrees are possible across the

area on Friday. Please refer to the Heat Advisory for more

details. 



A few strong to marginally severe thunderstorms are possible

Friday night. The strongest storms will be capable of producing

hail up to quarter size and wind gusts to 60 mph. 



Scattered thunderstorm chances continue Saturday through 

Wednesday night. The highest chances for rain will be Saturday

night through Sunday night. Details regarding thunderstorm 

coverage and intensity remain uncertain.



&&



More information may be obtained at the following web page:

   https://www.weather.gov/hastings



