Washington-Webster-Wheeler-White-Whitfield-Wilcox-Wilkes-

Wilkinson-

912 PM EDT Thu Aug 7 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for north and central Georgia.



.DAY ONE...Tonight...



No hazardous weather is expected at this time.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday...



Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected across the

mountains of north Georgia and in east central Georgia Friday

afternoon. 



Daily thunderstorm activity will increase in Georgia through

Monday. Storms will continue between Tuesday and Wednesday, but

overall coverage should decrease each day. Severe weather is 

unlikely, but a few storms may produce locally heavy rainfall. 



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation is not requested but spotters are encouraged 

to submit reports of severe weather through the web by going to 

weather.gov/atlanta.  Please relay any information about observed severe

weather to the NWS.



$$



