Spot Forecast for Adobe Mtn. Wildfire...EIDC

National Weather Service Elko NV

617 PM PDT Thu Aug 7 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1900 PDT on August 07. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



Please contact National Weather Service Elko if you have questions

or concerns with this forecast.



...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM PDT THIS EVENING...



.DISCUSSION...Sustained W-SW winds of 15-25 mph with gusts up to 

30 mph will continue through this evening. Winds will shift after 

midnight to WNW with speeds dropping to 5-10 mph which will 

continue through the overnight. Friday morning winds will be light

out of the NW at 5 MPH, shifting to the WNW with speeds 

increasing to 10-15 mph with gusts up to 25 mph trough the late 

afternoon. winds will drop to 5 to 15 mph through about 10 PM 

Friday evening when a front pushing south out of Idaho reaches the

area. This boundary will for a few hours increase wind speeds 

back to 10-20 mph with a few gusts up to 30 mph, while wind 

direction changes to be from the NE. Winds will remain out of the 

NE but speeds will fall to 5-10 mph after 2 am Saturday morning.



