Okfuskee OK-Okmulgee OK-Osage OK-Ottawa OK-Pawnee OK-Pittsburg OK-

Pushmataha OK-Rogers OK-Sebastian AR-Sequoyah OK-Tulsa OK-Wagoner OK-

Washington OK-Washington AR-

818 PM CDT Thu Aug 7 2025



This Outlook is for Northwest and West Central Arkansas as well as

much of Eastern Oklahoma.



.DAY ONE...Tonight.



No hazardous weather is expected at this time.



SPOTTER AND EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT ACTION STATEMENT...

Spotter Activation Not Expected.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Friday through Wednesday.

FRIDAY...High Wind...Dangerous Heat Potential. 

SATURDAY and SUNDAY...Dangerous Heat Potential. 

MONDAY through WEDNESDAY...Thunderstorm Potential.



EXTENDED DISCUSSION...



Hot and humid conditions will continue into next week. Afternoon 

heat index values will likely exceed 105 degrees across much of 

eastern Oklahoma and west central Arkansas Friday through Sunday,

with a slight drop off in heat index values into early next week.

Some locations may experience very dangerous heat index values

exceeding 110 degrees locally on Friday. Low thunderstorm chances

may also return to parts of the area next week.



weather.gov/tulsa contains additional information.



$$



